      "notes": "Issue #245. Severity (info/success/warning/error) and disposition (shown/dismissed) are separate axes from the region state the parity harness compares: the contract reuses REGION_STATES rather than forking a second list. Dismissal removes the notice from the live region instead of adding a sixth region state, because a dismissed notice that still occupied a region would still be announced. Only `error` is aria-live assertive; `warning` stays polite so cautions do not train users to ignore the region. The queue is bounded and errors are never silently dropped. Opt-in and non-primary: the stock n8n notification presentation remains the default path.",
